Hi everyone,

@reporter  not sure if this is related to your issue, but I have very similar setups (streamlit in docker running behind a nginx) and ran into a similar error. 
I have like a 'standard nginx config'  that I use for all deployments that looks like:

```nginx
server {
        server_name ****;

        location / {
                proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:42001/;
        }

        location ^~ /static {
                proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:42001/static/;
        }

        location ^~ /healthz {
                proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:42001/healthz;
        }

        location ^~ /vendor {
                proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:42001/vendor;
        }

        location /stream {
                proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:42001/stream;
                proxy_http_version 1.1;
                proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
                proxy_set_header Host $host;
                proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
                proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
                proxy_read_timeout 86400;
        }


    listen 443 ssl; # managed by Certbot
    ssl_certificate ********/fullchain.pem; # managed by Certbot
    ssl_certificate_key ********/privkey.pem; # managed by Certbot
    include /etc/letsencrypt/options-ssl-nginx.conf; # managed by Certbot
    ssl_dhparam /etc/letsencrypt/ssl-dhparams.pem; # managed by Certbot

}

server {
    if ($host = ********) {
        return 301 https://$host$request_uri;
    } # managed by Certbot


        server_name ********;
    listen 80;
}
```

That proved working for some time now, but with the latest version of streamlit, a new deployment threw the same error as you describe. To me it seems like streamlit rebuilt some stuff regarding the usage of websockets. I tried to add the websocket proxy pass configuration to the `location /` like:

```nginx
location / {
                proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:42004/;
                proxy_set_header        Host $host;
                proxy_set_header        X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
                proxy_set_header        X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
                proxy_set_header        X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
                proxy_http_version 1.1;
                proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
                proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
        }
``` 

I am not a websocket expert and also not really sure what I did, but for me that did the trick and now also the container shipping with the latest streamlit version works fine.

Works on my machine.

I'm running Streamlit with `--server.enableCORS=false --server.enableXsrfProtection=false`
I think it started working when I set this line `proxy_set_header Connection $connection_upgrade;`

Here's my nginx.conf
```
map $http_upgrade $connection_upgrade {
default upgrade;
‘’ close;
